academy-id "q-102320" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}}=\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "597b62cc-0411-5d21-9e4a-c7aa35afe536" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373978} {:answer/id #uuid "8c4e9d7e-9a9c-5ab0-ba07-f9a6ee7cd7ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373979} {:answer/id #uuid "3defc4b7-25d0-55bb-a000-0668706acf2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373980} {:answer/id #uuid "71d4c007-dd7c-540e-9267-a01530115175" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373981} {:answer/id #uuid "15eecdc9-81b8-5fa4-991b-46cac7d3ce91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373982}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "15eecdc9-81b8-5fa4-991b-46cac7d3ce91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373982} :answer-field/id #uuid "f414bdee-ec8f-5e43-be41-e29fb714b1b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6131bff9-6164-5597-92ad-816d41332955" :question/math-academy-id "q-102339" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $6{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-6 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-9)\\cdot 4+8\\cdot 2}{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-36+16}{16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{-20}{20} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n6{x}_{1}=6\\cdot (-1)=-6.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186157707 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2eb558b-1ca9-53ca-9ae0-01206db1624a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155495} {:answer/id #uuid "fb503f1e-78b0-5952-ad31-8a812b9e7731" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155496} {:answer/id #uuid "1b751b2f-9f9b-5bb2-8014-bc97fccbe96e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155497} {:answer/id #uuid "1cfc75e8-923d-50b5-80de-e91d8e048a99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155498} {:answer/id #uuid "23c6c26d-e00b-59bf-a5a8-733d85a8246b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23c6c26d-e00b-59bf-a5a8-733d85a8246b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155499} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ba306e3-984c-5a9f-8493-06058695649e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186155494}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58dd07d7-85f8-5406-9b6d-4dde047be9a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-39400" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $29{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -17\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 4+2\\cdot (-2)}{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{15-4-4}{9+16+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n29{x}_{1}=29\\cdot \\frac{7}{29}=7.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373983 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "15b92bed-c97f-5b87-9811-fbfc5c03314d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Component of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthogonal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84747dcd-04cb-5d65-9f3c-c9ac8abcaa95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373985} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd8b248-0c00-5c1f-a385-5cdb2d41eb40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373986} {:answer/id #uuid "92e5dbd1-9177-53cb-9588-a9f53d8c7437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373987} {:answer/id #uuid "899db367-7eba-5d21-a346-1b2c40960edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373988} {:answer/id #uuid "35703d0c-c0a7-59ce-8870-fe751db1443c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "899db367-7eba-5d21-a346-1b2c40960edd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373988} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c9f79f-bc1e-51b0-8fbc-b1cf3db45af3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373984}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9fbd1e5c-f59b-5839-83e8-2af28c44549a" :question/math-academy-id "q-81104" :question/problem "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $20{x}_{2},$ where ${x}_{2}$ is the second component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{2},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)\\cdot (-2)+1\\cdot (-1)}{(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-1}{4+1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n20{x}_{2}=20\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}=4.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373990 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "39b12711-22c8-5cb7-bd61-e128734e7e6f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Components of a Vector With Respect to a Given Orthonormal Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3bcf4d31-6408-582e-b8c3-21a1b2e0df2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373992} {:answer/id #uuid "762055fc-438e-5f70-ae0f-22ffe3258e9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373993} {:answer/id #uuid "5ac362d8-bd18-5d68-9f2a-92f7f4048578" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373994} {:answer/id #uuid "55c1c309-dd75-5c9a-8cee-dc946fbaa7f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373995} {:answer/id #uuid "2a34048a-175b-56e5-834f-5f9ef688a144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373996}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55c1c309-dd75-5c9a-8cee-dc946fbaa7f7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373995} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc5b1465-11dd-5e44-b855-e0ca6e43892b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373991}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c992dc2c-cb54-59b3-b528-1c122228a4e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-81141" :question/problem "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B$ of ${R}^{3}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}$, where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{35}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{35}}\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2},\\,{q}_{3}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =x\\cdot {q}_{1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{10} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{10}}{2}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}} \\\\ \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{10}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-2)=-1.\n$$"}]}
